novel/chapters/ch-01/scenes/s-002.md:9:"We go around—under the bridge repair, like we planned," I tell Jun, because plans are the cords that keep a kingdom from falling apart. He nods, fingers worrying the flashlight in his pocket. The tin thumps against his spine in the pack; I can feel the velvet pouch against my thigh where the brooch sits, a small warm weight I do not let go of.
novel/chapters/ch-01/scenes/s-001.md:5:I hold it and let the sun warm the metal. "A dented tin lunchbox, its knight's paint flaked at the edges, smelling faintly of tomato and pennies; inside, a paper-wrapped sandwich and a small velvet pouch." The words taste like instructions. I slide the pouch closer to my palm, feel the thrift-shop cool of silver beneath the fabric.
